From 9aa2d223e9d3fe30c1d26451fd72c6bb53ecb317 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ritvik <ritvik2014@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 21:49:44 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 05/38] render: liquid glass for lumen (lumen-glass-v1)

A private protocol (resources/lumen-glass-v1.xml): a client describes its
glass as rounded boxes (continuous or circular corners) with refraction,
dispersion, bevel and specular, plus merge/frost/saturation, double-buffered
on wl_surface.commit. Layer surfaces with glass get one framebuffer capture
over the shapes' bounding box (this frame's backdrop, no client capture),
drawn through liquid_glass.frag: squircle SDF, smooth union, inward lensing
along a circular bevel profile, per-channel dispersion, rim light.
